# Jeni IDE Environment Configuration

Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in your values.
(`.env.local` is not committed to git for security reasons)

## Required Configuration

# Your OpenRouter API key
# Get one at: https://openrouter.ai/keys
JENI_LLM_API_KEY=sk-or-v1-your-key-here

## Optional Configuration

# LLM API endpoint (defaults to OpenRouter)
# JENI_LLM_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1

# Model to use (defaults to Laguna S 2.1)
# JENI_LLM_MODEL=poolside/laguna-s-2.1:free

## How to Use

### Option 1: Environment Variable (Recommended for Development)

Set the variable before running dev:

**Windows (PowerShell):**
```powershell
$env:JENI_LLM_API_KEY="sk-or-v1-your-key"
npm run dev
```

**Linux/Mac (bash):**
```bash
JENI_LLM_API_KEY=sk-or-v1-your-key npm run dev
```

### Option 2: .env.local File

1. Copy this file to `.env.local`:
   ```
   cp .env.example .env.local
   ```

2. Edit `.env.local` and add your API key

3. Run Jeni:
   ```
   npm run dev
   ```

## Important Security Notes

- The API key must NEVER be exposed to the React renderer
- The API key must NEVER be logged or displayed in error messages
- The API key must NEVER be committed to git
- The API key is only used in the Electron main process
- .env.local is in .gitignore

## Supported Providers

The LLM client is OpenAI-compatible, so you can use:

- **OpenRouter** (default) — https://openrouter.ai
- **OpenAI** — https://platform.openai.com
- **Anthropic Claude** — https://console.anthropic.com
- Local LLMs with OpenAI-compatible interfaces

Just change the JENI_LLM_BASE_URL and JENI_LLM_MODEL.

## Default Configuration

**Provider:** OpenRouter  
**Base URL:** https://openrouter.ai/api/v1  
**Model:** poolside/laguna-s-2.1:free (fast, free tier)

## Troubleshooting

**"LLM not configured" error:**
- Check that JENI_LLM_API_KEY is set
- Make sure there are no typos in the key
- Restart `npm run dev` after setting the variable

**"Invalid API key" response:**
- Verify your OpenRouter API key is correct
- Check it at https://openrouter.ai/keys
- Make sure your account has credits

**Network/Connection errors:**
- Check your internet connection
- Verify OpenRouter is accessible
- Check firewall/proxy settings

